We can use trimesh intersection boolean at transformed states. Also min distance use trimesh.proximity.closest_point on surfaces sampling. Exact min distance not necessary; can use BVH nearest. `trimesh.proximity.ProximityQuery(mesh).on_surface(vertices_of_other)` gives point-to-surface, but min between surfaces via vertices only approximate; with fine mesh okay. For collisions, boolean intersection volume > tiny.

Need design in OpenSCAD then render. Let's write initial model.scad systematically. Could write Python to generate some geometry? Better hardcode SCAD with functions. Need use `$fn=72` or special variables per module.

OpenSCAD 3D hull with scaled spheres. Need be careful `scale([sx,sy,sz]) sphere(r=1)`.

Let's define:
```
$fn=72;
tailT=7.0;
...
module ell(c,r){ translate(c) scale(r) sphere(r=1); } // r vector
module sph(c,r){ translate(c) sphere(r=r); }
```

Body:
```
module body_fixed(){
  union(){
    // torso etc
    ell([-2,0,21],[16,10.5,10.5]);
    ell([10,0,22],[8.5,10,9]);
    ell([-14,0,24],[8,9,8.5]);
    hull(){ ell([-17,0,28],[7,8,7]); ell([-24,0,37],[6.5,7.5,6.5]); }
    // head
    ell([-28.5,0,44],[8.5,8.3,8.5]);
    ell([-34.5,0,41],[4.4,5.4,4.2]);
    // lower jaw
    ell([-34.5,0,38.6],[4.0,4.8,2.2]);
    // maybe crest
    ...
    // legs
    four_legs();
    // tail pillar connector
    tail_stock();
    // spikes
    ...
    // connector & boss at J1
    translate([J1x,0,0]) parent_boss();
    translate([J1x-5.8,-1.5,0]) cube([5.8,3,7.0]);
  }
}
```
Potential issue parent boss at J1 and connector are union with body pillar, but pillar max x16.2, J1=22, connector starts16.2 length5.8 to22. Exact. Good. If pillar top/hull x at z<7 is <=16.2; need ensure. Tail_stock ell max16.2.

