Let's plan module hierarchy:

```
part="all";
tailT=7.0; ...
module c_ring_2d(){...}
module child_ring(){ // at origin, bottom z=0
 difference(){
  linear_extrude(tailT) c_ring_2d();
  cylinder(h=1.5,r1=4.2,r2=2.7);
 }
}
module parent_boss(){...}
module link_body_2d(jw,jb) { ... } // only C ring + body to before next, no boss
module tail_link(jw,jb) {
 union(){
  translate([jw,0,0]) child_ring();
  linear_extrude(tailT) difference(){
    union(){ hull... } 
    translate([jb,0]) circle(5.7);
  }
  // connector to east boss (box), plus boss
  translate([jb-6.5,-1.5,0]) cube([6.5,3,tailT]);
  translate([jb,0,0]) parent_boss();
  // dorsal fin
 }
}
```
But `linear_extrude` includes ring separately; body 2D starts near jw. Need all body z0..7. The C ring child has z0..7 with recess. We should not extrude body over the recess (body starts jw+2.2 but could overlap ring footprint at x>jw). It's at radius>2.2 but if within r4.2 at z0, it could fill the child recess, breaking capture! Critical: any child material inside recess cone must be removed, not just ring. The body attaches to ring at x~jw+4.5, within outer ring. At z0, recess radius4.2 around pivot; body could extend into r<4.2 at z0, filling the flange cavity. Need subtract the conical recess after unioning all child geometry, locally around the west pivot. So build child link union (ring + body + fins) then subtract cone at jw (z0..1.5 r4.2->2.7) globally. This also removes any body material inside, leaving ring conical recess. Good.
Also hole: subtract cylinder r2.7 through z0..tailT at west pivot after union, in case body intrudes. C ring already. Build:
```
difference(){
  union(){
    translate(jw) linear_extrude(tailT) c_ring_solid_2d(); // difference circle - opening, no hole? 
    linear_extrude(tailT) body_2d_with_clearance;
    connector...
    boss...
    fins...
  }
  translate(jw) {
    cylinder(h=tailT+1, r=2.7);
    // actually cone recess below and hole above
    cylinder(h=1.5, r1=4.2,r2=2.7);
  }
}
```
But subtraction at west pivot would also cut the parent's own boss if west? No, parent boss is at east. Good.
Need C ring 2D outer with opening but no inner hole; union body; subtract hole. Great. `c_sector_2d()` = circle(5.2) minus opening wedge only (solid disk sector). Then final subtract cylinder hole and cone.
For Tail3, no east boss, same.

But if we union body shape after east clearance, the connector box and parent boss at east are part of same part. The child C ring cut at west only; no effect east. Good.

At J2, child C ring belongs to tail2, parent boss at east of tail1. Parent ring? none. Fine.

For each tail link, the east parent boss is built. At its west, subtract cone.

Need avoid subtracting hole at west after adding dorsal fins etc; fine.

Parent boss position east; top head cone. The child link body at east may overlap own boss? The connector intentionally. But child link body extends maybe to jb-5.8 due clearance; connector from jb-6.5. fine.

